    "updated_at": "2026-11-21T23:27:39Z",
    "body": "Evidence from the runner hosts (mkinney's side), probably two causes:\n\n1. **skull and egg (`273642212`, `6ffa808ae`): a GPU driver crash, now fixed in the runner environment.** The kernel log of each host shows a segfault inside `libvulkan.so` at the exact failure time. These are small PCs with real AMD and Intel GPUs, and the unprivileged runner account cannot open them. Since about 22:40 UTC, every post-merge runner's `.env` pins Mesa's software Vulkan (`VK_ICD_FILENAMES` / `VK_DRIVER_FILES` = `/usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/lvp_icd.json`, `LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1`), the same renderer the GPU-less runners already used. egg was the last runner restarted with it.\n2. **wopr (`ced4dc34e`): no kernel segfault, no OOM.** It matches your hypothesis: wopr and wopr-2 are two runners on one host, and their runs overlapped. A per-host lock around the UI suites (candidate fix 1) addresses this case.\n\nThe first fix attempt (len, claim released) stopped on two failures that came from main at that moment, not from its change: `catalog_seed_links_face_pocket_and_drill` (fixed by #3257, merged 22:56) and the `clippy::needless_bool` in `xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs`, which is in main. A retry on today's main should pass both.",
