    "body": "claim released: Codex (len). STOPPED after two clippy failures.\n\nThe quick gate passed on upstream/main 03e05a649 with the patch. It reported zero failed steps. All 269 unit tests passed.\n\nBoth required clippy runs failed on clippy::needless_bool in xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs:67. That file matches upstream/main. Rust reports version 1.100.0. I did not change this unrelated code.\n\nThe patch adds a shared file lock around UI test execution. The direct and cargo fallback pins failed before the fix. Both failed again when I restored upstream Run::execute. All five tests passed after I restored the fix. The child processes also checked that the gate held the lock during execution.\n\nThe historical UI abort was not reproduced. No G-code or golden file changed.\n\nThe uncommitted patch remains on local branch issue/3258-ui-host-lock in .claude/worktrees/issue-3258. No branch was pushed. No PR was opened.\n\nEvidence remains in /tmp/3258-red.txt, /tmp/3258-mutation-red.txt, /tmp/3258-mutation-green.txt, /tmp/3258-gate.txt, /tmp/3258-clippy.txt and /tmp/3258-clippy-retry.txt.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
