    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T07:20:55Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/3258-parallel-gate-isolation · PR #3302 · pinned by exit_status::tests::a_crashed_step_executable_says_how_it_stopped_in_its_log_and_note · merges when reviewed\n\nRoot cause, with evidence:\n- The three UI failures were signal deaths, not a resource that the repository shares between runs. `exit -1` is the gate's value for a process with no exit code.\n- In each red log, the tests that did not finish are the GPU tests. In trace_parity they are `the_gpu_sees_the_box_the_cpu_sees` and `deviation_classes_agree_with_the_cpu_verdict`. In egui_app they are the three headless-draw tests.\n- This agrees with the `libvulkan.so` segfaults in the kernel logs of skull and egg. All three failures came before the software Vulkan pin (about 22:40 UTC). About 30 post-merge runs came after the pin, many at the same time, and none has this signature.\n- The uma `bore_core` failure was the shared `/tmp` PID directory. #3290 fixed it.\n\nThe PR adds no host lock. It makes the gate write the signal or crash status into the step log and the note, for example `exit -1 (killed by signal 11 (SIGSEGV))`. If a UI step dies again on software Vulkan, the log then names the signal, and the held host-lock patch is the next step. The skull hang (44982953354) is not covered.\n",
